Changes from version 1.1 to version 1.2:
*****************************************

Emulator:

1: Bit 21 in the Exception register implemented, without any effect on
   floting point precision (used bu the Gier emulator for RC4000).



Changes from version 1.0 to version 1.1:
*****************************************

Emulator:

1: RC433X and RC433XRAM devices added. Autoload by emulator possible.

2: Bug fix: In connection with QEMM's STEALTH feature (and maybe also in
   other envirenments), unpredictable things happened upon leaving the
   emulator. Corrected.

There might be other changes of minor importance that I forgot about...

Monitor:

1: The monitor supplied as a DOS file supports up to 8 RC433X discs. The
   STDMONITOR still supports up to 6 RC4819 discs.


Changes from version 0.1T to version 1.0:
*****************************************

Emulator:

1: Bug fix: In some cases, virtual disc contents were damaged due to an error
   in the logic taking care of extending the disc image files. If a disc
   image file with an illegal size is found, it is repaired at start-up, and
   an informative message is given.

2: Design bug fix: Disc transfers with a block size of more than 511 segments
   were not performed properly. This was due to the fact that a real RC4000
   has max. 128 kw core store. The virtual DFC 403 disc controller has been 
   modified to allow block sizes up to 4095 segments, as this is the limit
   that the monitor will handle properply.

3: Bug fix: In rare cases, the emulator would report timer resolution=25.6 ms,
   although the PC was not a PS/2 system.


4: Handling of non-standard video modes and screen attributes has
   been enhanced.

5: Frequency of the "beep" used for input prompt has been changed to 1000 Hz.
   A problem concerning the duration of the beep is fixed.

6: The configuration file can be located in the same directory as RC4000.EXE
   without having to state the full path in the RC4000CFG environment string.

   

Monitor:

1: Monitor procedures Own Process Description (5),Test Event (66),
   and Send Pseudo Message (124) included.

2: Device list slightly changed.

3: The monitor will not waste time making dummy-settings of protection
   key in the entire process area each time a process is started. Has
   influence on performance when using the SOS operating system.


Other:

1: In the SOS system (bsos) included, a bug has been fixed. The bug could
   cause a crash of RC4000 on certain process / bs configurations. The reason
   was that SOS tried to handle process relocation, although this is not
   possible on RC4000.

2: Max. core size set to 1 MHW in RC4000.CFG.


Known problems:
***************

1: The Alt-D function (supposed to autotype date and time) sometimes returns
   garbage.

2: Reading and writing address marks on RC4819 discs does not work:
   Writing has no effect; reading returns wrong contents.

3: The (undocumented) trace and single step facilities has (maybe?) a problem
   with the je instruction.

